<task id="075" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Build the record-aware container resolver: a secure record resolves to its OWN sprk_containerid, everything else to the BU cascade, absent secure container fails closed</title>
    <phase>0c Secure Documents — Wave 2</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>This is the seam the entire document-isolation guarantee rests on. Provisioning already stamps the container; this is the component that makes the stamp mean something.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Architectural seam consumed by 7+ client sites and server ingest, in both directions (record→container for reads/writes, container→record for task 073). Getting the shape wrong propagates everywhere.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <effort-reason>Brownfield with three existing resolution strategies, a client/server split constrained by INV-7, and a bidirectional mapping requirement.</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>wave2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Introduces a shared Infrastructure seam consumed by task 073 and task 076; concurrent edits would fork the mapping.</parallel-reason>
