    <tags>bff-api, api, dataverse, security</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Filed 2026-08-25. Verified: NO server-side path reads `sprk_containerid` off an `sprk_project` row other than provisioning's own guard. Task 021 stamps it; nothing consumes it. Confirmed live: three existing projects carry the ROOT BU's container id, identical to `SharePointEmbedded__DefaultContainerId`.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Provisioning gives every secure project its own SPE container and writes the id to the project row. Nothing reads it. Build the one resolver that decides which container a document belongs to — the record's own for secure records, the BU cascade otherwise — and make an absent secure container a hard failure rather than a fallback.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform engineer. Designing a seam that many callers will depend on, and that must be impossible to bypass by accident.</role>

  <goal>One shared, record-aware container resolver exists and is the only way any code decides which container to use. A secure record resolves to its own container or fails; it never resolves to a shared one. The same mapping answers the reverse question (container → owning record) for task 073.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>WHY THIS IS THE WHOLE GUARANTEE. SharePoint Embedded permissions are **additive-only** — verified against current Microsoft documentation 2026-08-25: *"SharePoint Embedded content inherits permissions from its container hierarchy. You can't break inheritance on arbitrary files or folders."* This is the same shape as Dataverse's no-per-record-deny. **You cannot make a document inside a shared container invisible to that container's members.** Therefore a secure project's documents MUST live in their own container; there is no per-item alternative. This makes design §5.1c load-bearing, not an optimisation.

THE THREE EXISTING STRATEGIES (design §5.1c):
1. **Acting user's BU** → `businessunit.sprk_containerid`. 7 client sites; canonical client resolver `xrmProvider.getSpeContainerIdFromBusinessUnit`. The BFF deliberately does NOT resolve this server-side (INV-7). → **needs the secure special case**
2. **A single global `ArchiveContainerId`** from config — server-side email/communication ingest (`IncomingCommunicationProcessor`). → **needs the secure special case, and is the one easiest to forget** because it has no client and no wizard
3. **The document's own `GraphDriveId`/`GraphItemId`** — every read/download path once a document exists. → **no change needed**

Strategy 3 is fine. Strategies 1 and 2 both need the special case, and today neither has it — which is why secure content lands in shared containers.

THE RULE: *if the context record is a secure record, use its own `sprk_containerid`; otherwise the existing BU cascade.* `sprk_issecure` exists on exactly three entities (verified from live attribute metadata 2026-08-25): `sprk_project`, `sprk_matter`, `sprk_workassignment`. Derive that list from metadata, not from this paragraph.

FAIL CLOSED, AND THIS IS THE POINT. A secure record whose `sprk_containerid` is null must produce a hard failure — never a fallback to the BU or archive container. A silent fallback is precisely the isolation failure this task exists to remove, and it would be invisible: the upload would succeed.

INV-7 AND THE CLIENT/SERVER SPLIT. Strategy 1's resolver is deliberately client-side. Respect that: the shared component may need a client half and a server half. What must NOT happen is two independent implementations of the secure special case that can drift. Give strategy 2 a server-side equivalent of the same decision.

BIDIRECTIONAL. Task 073 needs container → owning record to authorize uploads. Build the mapping so both directions come from one place. Coordinate; do not let 073 build a second mapping.

DO NOT ADD THE `issecure` TEST AT SEVEN CLIENT SITES — that is seven places to drift. Route every call site through the resolver (that routing work is task 076).

ALSO IN SCOPE FOR AWARENESS: a client write-back at `src/solutions/DocumentUploadWizard/sprk_subgrid_commands.js` overwrites `sprk_project.sprk_containerid` with the BU container when the field is not on the form. Even a correct resolver is defeated by that. Task 076 owns suppressing the wizard cascade; flag anything you find here.</background>
