  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">A secure record with no container FAILS CLOSED and loudly. Never fall back to the BU cascade or the archive container for a secure record. This is the single most important behaviour in the task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="build-plan">ONE resolver. Not a client copy and a server copy of the decision — a shared decision with, if INV-7 requires, two thin call sites. State how drift is prevented.</constraint>
    <constraint source="build-plan">Bidirectional: record → container AND container → owning record, from one mapping, so task 073 consumes it rather than reimplementing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Derive the securable-entity list from live metadata (`sprk_issecure` present), not from a hard-coded list. A fourth securable entity must not silently bypass the resolver.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT put the `issecure` test at individual call sites. The whole point is one decision point.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">SPE access goes through the `SpeFileStore` facade; do not inject Graph types outside Infrastructure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">State the Placement Justification for any new BFF component; verify publish size (≤60 MB, baseline 45.05 MB) and CVE scan.</constraint>
  </constraints>

